  "summary": "Recent preprints report 103.96 Tb/s on-chip coherent-lite links and parameter-efficient unitary layers for coherent optical neural networks.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is coherent optical processing built on programmable unitary interferometric hardware. The first preprint applies coherent-style detection to on-chip interconnects, combining wavelength and mode multiplexing with self-homodyne detection to reach an aggregate line rate of 103.96 Tb/s. The other two preprints target unitary transformations directly. One proposes a logarithmic-depth butterfly interferometer architecture for parameter-efficient unitary transformations in coherent optical neural networks. The other proposes a modular photonic processor built from unitary tiles of fixed mixers and programmable phases, evaluated by numerical fitting. What is new is the joint emphasis on multidimensional multiplexing, depth-efficient parameterization, and modular tiling of unitary elements for both communication and computation.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-haiku-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-18"
